+- 2026-06-11: EFFICIENCY axis confirmation (north-star §5): the model-free GAP-4 verifier (demo-fit + restricted-namespace execution + content-hash match, ~0.11s/task, $0) vs an LLM-judge selecting from the SAME ARC candidate sets -- accuracy parity at what cost ratio? The verifier-as-COMMODITY framing (Deep Think Q1: necessary but zero-margin) makes the efficiency number the honest value statement: the gate is cheap AND lossless, so it earns its place on EFFICIENCY even though it is not a smart selector. Confirm/extend .371's exp4013 if it landed; otherwise run fresh. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=success: verifier_parity_wallclock_95.3x_judge_over_verifier; results/experiment_4026_verifier_vs_judge_efficiency.json
